 "text": "At first, everything takes longer. Finding your clothes. Pouring water. Reaching for a door handle. Things you once did without thinking suddenly require attention. And contrary to what movies suggest, your other senses don't instantly become superhuman. But you can learn to pay attention to information that was always there. And one particular sound is about to change how you understand space.",
